This leans into the identity-first brand you’ve been building while keeping the product claims grounded. I wrote it to feel cinematic rather than loud.

Wild Hawg Energy

30-Second Brand Film — “Remember”

Length: 30 seconds

⸻

Scene 1 — Dawn (0–4 sec)

Black screen.

A slow heartbeat.

An alarm sounds.

A hand reaches out…

…then pauses.

Voiceover:

“Every day asks the same question.”

⸻

Scene 2 — Choice (4–8 sec)

Quick cuts:

* Boots hitting the floor.
* Running shoes tied.
* Coffee maker ignored.
* A bag of Wild Hawg Energy picked up instead.

The bag tears open.

A gummy.

A grin.

Voiceover:

“Who are you going to be today?”

⸻

Scene 3 — Momentum (8–18 sec)

Fast, energetic montage.

* Early morning lift.
* Dirt trail run.
* Building something in a garage.
* Whiteboard full of ideas.
* Dad playing with his kids.
* Friend getting helped move.
* Sunrise over water.
* Someone crossing “Done” off a list.

No superheroes.

Just people choosing action.

Voiceover:

“Energy isn’t about being louder.”

“It’s about showing up.”

“Again.”

⸻

Scene 4 — Identity (18–25 sec)

Close-up.

Someone quietly hands another person a bag of Wild Hawg.

No speech.

Just a nod.

The other smiles.

Voiceover:

“The strongest people don’t wait for motivation.”

“They build momentum.”

⸻

Scene 5 — Closing (25–30 sec)

The bag stands on a workbench.

Sunlight cuts across the logo.

Simple.

Clean.

Bold.

Voiceover:

“Remember who you are.”

On screen:

WILD HAWG ENERGY

REWILD YOUR DAY.

